{{also|unilatéral}}
==English==

===Etymology===
A modern creation (c. 1802), from New Latin {{term|unilateralis||one-sidely, one-sided|lang=la}}, from {{term|unus||one|lang=la}} + {{term|lateralis||sided, lateral|lang=la}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# done by one [[side]] only
# affecting only one side of the body
# binding or affecting one party only

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|onesidedly}}
* {{l|en|one-sidely}}

